{"event": "tool_call", "t": 1795229760.053, "name": "report", "arguments": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "int_sales__orders_enriched -> customer_ltv (new)", "summary": "Cancelled orders were counted as revenue. The status field mixes case ('CANCELLED' and 'cancelled'), and cancelled_at is null for most cancelled orders, so the is_cancelled flag (driven only by cancelled_at) misses them. The existing LTV logic in dim_customers and int_customers__lifetime_metrics relies on that flag, which overstates LTV."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "main.int_sales__orders_enriched grouped by status", "finding": "Cancelled-like statuses appear in mixed case: 'CANCELLED' 199 orders (all without ship/delivery dates, only 24 with cancelled_at) and 'cancelled' in lowercase in both SAP and POS. is_cancelled is true only where cancelled_at is set, so most cancelled orders were counted."}, {"kind": "lineage", "ref": "models/marts/core/dim_customers.sql", "finding": "Existing LTV uses sum(grand_total) filtered by is_cancelled = false, with a comment noting refunds are not excluded. It is the replacement for the deprecated rpt_customer_ltv_v1."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.dim_status_codes (ORDER entity)", "finding": "CANCELLED is a terminal order status, so it should not count as revenue. REFUNDED is also a terminal status, but no REFUNDED rows appear in the order statuses."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.customer_ltv reconciliation", "finding": "customer_ltv has 1035 rows, one per customer from int_customers__unified, with no duplicate customer_id. Sum of lifetime_value = 7,447,108.62, which equals the sum of grand_total over non-cancelled orders in int_sales__orders_enriched (all grand_total sum 8,032,619.31). total_orders sums to 2436 valid orders. 656 customers are 'No Value'."}, {"kind": "log", "ref": "run_dbt customer_ltv", "finding": "Build succeeded (1 model, success=1)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql", "summary": "New table model producing main.customer_ltv. One row per customer from int_customers__unified. Aggregates grand_total over orders where upper(trim(status)) <> 'CANCELLED' and cancelled_at is null. Output columns: customer_id, total_orders (integer), lifetime_value, avg_order_value (decimal rounded to 2), first/last_order_date (date), value_segment using the specified thresholds. Customers with no valid orders get 0 / 'No Value'. Upstream models and tests were not changed."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "duration_s": 132.08, "output_chars": 104, "is_error": false}
