{"event": "attempt_end", "t": 1795229880.914, "attempt": 1, "passed": true, "failed_check": null, "checks": [{"name": "tamper", "passed": true, "detail": "1 changed file(s), all allowed; all 929 test(s) unchanged"}, {"name": "masking", "passed": true, "detail": "no model disabled, no rows filtered away"}, {"name": "clean_rebuild", "passed": true, "detail": "dbt build passed: 2871 node(s); 293 node(s) that already failed before the change, none downstream of it, still fail: model.retail_dw_master.COMP_OPERATIONS_YOY; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__mom; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__qoq; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__wow; model.retail_dw_master.comp_customers__yoy; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__mom; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__qoq; model.retail_dw_master.comp_finance__wow; and 285 more; 1 node(s) skipped behind an old failure upstream were built on their own"}, {"name": "collateral", "passed": true, "detail": "2212 model(s) outside the lineage unchanged (222 compared by row count only and 0 not compared, because they differ between builds of the unchanged project)"}], "duration_s": 131.7, "diff": "diff --git a/models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql b/models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+{{\n+    config(\n+        materialized='table',\n+        tags=['mart', 'customers', 'ltv']\n+    )\n+}}\n+\n+-- customer_ltv\n+-- Corrected customer lifetime value. Only orders that resulted in revenue count:\n+-- cancelled orders are excluded. Status is matched case-insensitively because the\n+-- source mixes 'CANCELLED' and 'cancelled', and cancelled_at is not populated for\n+-- most cancelled orders, so the is_cancelled flag alone misses them.\n+\n+with customers as (\n+\n+    select distinct customer_id\n+    from {{ ref('int_customers__unified') }}\n+    where customer_id is not null\n+\n+),\n+\n+valid_orders as (\n+\n+    select\n+        customer_id,\n+        order_id,\n+        grand_total,\n+        ordered_at\n+    from {{ ref('int_sales__orders_enriched') }}\n+    where customer_id is not null\n+      and upper(trim(status)) <> 'CANCELLED'\n+      and cancelled_at is null\n+\n+),\n+\n+order_metrics as (\n+\n+    select\n+        customer_id,\n+        count(distinct order_id) as total_orders,\n+        sum(grand_total) as lifetime_value_raw,\n+        avg(grand_total) as avg_order_value_raw,\n+        cast(min(ordered_at) as date) as first_order_date,\n+        cast(max(ordered_at) as date) as last_order_date\n+    from valid_orders\n+    group by customer_id\n+\n+),\n+\n+final as (\n+\n+    select\n+        c.customer_id,\n+        coalesce(m.total_orders, 0)::integer as total_orders,\n+        round(coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0), 2)::decimal(18,2) as lifetime_value,\n+        round(coalesce(m.avg_order_value_raw, 0), 2)::decimal(18,2) as avg_order_value,\n+        m.first_order_date,\n+        m.last_order_date,\n+        case\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 1000 then 'VIP'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 500 then 'High Value'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 100 then 'Medium Value'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) > 0 then 'Low Value'\n+            else 'No Value'\n+        end::varchar as value_segment\n+    from customers c\n+    left join order_metrics m\n+        on c.customer_id = m.customer_id\n+\n+)\n+\n+select * from final\n"}
{"event": "report", "t": 1795229880.914, "claim": "fixed", "verdict": {"verdict": "fixed", "root_cause": {"category": "logic", "model": "int_sales__orders_enriched -> customer_ltv (new)", "summary": "Cancelled orders were counted as revenue. The status field mixes case ('CANCELLED' and 'cancelled'), and cancelled_at is null for most cancelled orders, so the is_cancelled flag (driven only by cancelled_at) misses them. The existing LTV logic in dim_customers and int_customers__lifetime_metrics relies on that flag, which overstates LTV."}, "evidence": [{"kind": "query", "ref": "main.int_sales__orders_enriched grouped by status", "finding": "Cancelled-like statuses appear in mixed case: 'CANCELLED' 199 orders (all without ship/delivery dates, only 24 with cancelled_at) and 'cancelled' in lowercase in both SAP and POS. is_cancelled is true only where cancelled_at is set, so most cancelled orders were counted."}, {"kind": "lineage", "ref": "models/marts/core/dim_customers.sql", "finding": "Existing LTV uses sum(grand_total) filtered by is_cancelled = false, with a comment noting refunds are not excluded. It is the replacement for the deprecated rpt_customer_ltv_v1."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.dim_status_codes (ORDER entity)", "finding": "CANCELLED is a terminal order status, so it should not count as revenue. REFUNDED is also a terminal status, but no REFUNDED rows appear in the order statuses."}, {"kind": "query", "ref": "main.customer_ltv reconciliation", "finding": "customer_ltv has 1035 rows, one per customer from int_customers__unified, with no duplicate customer_id. Sum of lifetime_value = 7,447,108.62, which equals the sum of grand_total over non-cancelled orders in int_sales__orders_enriched (all grand_total sum 8,032,619.31). total_orders sums to 2436 valid orders. 656 customers are 'No Value'."}, {"kind": "log", "ref": "run_dbt customer_ltv", "finding": "Build succeeded (1 model, success=1)."}], "changes": [{"path": "models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql", "summary": "New table model producing main.customer_ltv. One row per customer from int_customers__unified. Aggregates grand_total over orders where upper(trim(status)) <> 'CANCELLED' and cancelled_at is null. Output columns: customer_id, total_orders (integer), lifetime_value, avg_order_value (decimal rounded to 2), first/last_order_date (date), value_segment using the specified thresholds. Customers with no valid orders get 0 / 'No Value'. Upstream models and tests were not changed."}], "confidence": "medium"}, "diffs": [{"path": "models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql", "diff": "--- a/models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql\n+++ b/models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql\n@@ -0,0 +1,72 @@\n+{{\n+    config(\n+        materialized='table',\n+        tags=['mart', 'customers', 'ltv']\n+    )\n+}}\n+\n+-- customer_ltv\n+-- Corrected customer lifetime value. Only orders that resulted in revenue count:\n+-- cancelled orders are excluded. Status is matched case-insensitively because the\n+-- source mixes 'CANCELLED' and 'cancelled', and cancelled_at is not populated for\n+-- most cancelled orders, so the is_cancelled flag alone misses them.\n+\n+with customers as (\n+\n+    select distinct customer_id\n+    from {{ ref('int_customers__unified') }}\n+    where customer_id is not null\n+\n+),\n+\n+valid_orders as (\n+\n+    select\n+        customer_id,\n+        order_id,\n+        grand_total,\n+        ordered_at\n+    from {{ ref('int_sales__orders_enriched') }}\n+    where customer_id is not null\n+      and upper(trim(status)) <> 'CANCELLED'\n+      and cancelled_at is null\n+\n+),\n+\n+order_metrics as (\n+\n+    select\n+        customer_id,\n+        count(distinct order_id) as total_orders,\n+        sum(grand_total) as lifetime_value_raw,\n+        avg(grand_total) as avg_order_value_raw,\n+        cast(min(ordered_at) as date) as first_order_date,\n+        cast(max(ordered_at) as date) as last_order_date\n+    from valid_orders\n+    group by customer_id\n+\n+),\n+\n+final as (\n+\n+    select\n+        c.customer_id,\n+        coalesce(m.total_orders, 0)::integer as total_orders,\n+        round(coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0), 2)::decimal(18,2) as lifetime_value,\n+        round(coalesce(m.avg_order_value_raw, 0), 2)::decimal(18,2) as avg_order_value,\n+        m.first_order_date,\n+        m.last_order_date,\n+        case\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 1000 then 'VIP'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 500 then 'High Value'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) >= 100 then 'Medium Value'\n+            when coalesce(m.lifetime_value_raw, 0) > 0 then 'Low Value'\n+            else 'No Value'\n+        end::varchar as value_segment\n+    from customers c\n+    left join order_metrics m\n+        on c.customer_id = m.customer_id\n+\n+)\n+\n+select * from final\n"}], "text": "The verifier accepted the fix. I added a new `customer_ltv` model that excludes cancelled orders, which were being counted as revenue.\n\n**Root cause:** The existing LTV logic (`dim_customers`, `int_customers__lifetime_metrics`) relies on `is_cancelled`, which is set only when `cancelled_at` is populated. Cancelled orders appear in mixed case (`CANCELLED` and `cancelled`), and most have no `cancelled_at`, so they passed the filter and inflated LTV.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- In `int_sales__orders_enriched`, the `CANCELLED` status has 199 orders, but only 24 have `cancelled_at`. Lowercase `cancelled` also appears in both SAP and POS.\n- `dim_status_codes` lists CANCELLED as a terminal order status.\n- The new `main.customer_ltv` has 1,035 rows and no duplicate customers. Its `lifetime_value` total (7,447,108.62) matches the sum of `grand_total` over non-cancelled orders exactly. `total_orders` sums to 2,436.\n\n**Change:** `models/marts/core/customer_ltv.sql` (new table model). It takes one row per customer from `int_customers__unified`, left-joins the valid orders, and applies the required columns, rounding and segment thresholds. Upstream models and tests were not changed.\n\n**Open point:** I did not treat the abbreviated status `C` (about 285 orders) as cancelled. Its payment and shipping patterns don't clearly match cancelled orders, so I left it in. If `C` means cancelled in your source system, LTV would drop further. Confidence is medium for this reason."}
